{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '236,305p' ../agent-source/future.go; sed -n '1736,1813p' ../agent-source/raft.go; sed -n '990,1035p' ../agent-source/raft.go; sed -n '2050,2130p' ../agent-source/raft.go; sed -n '2163,2239p' ../agent-source/raft.go; grep -n '\"'^func'\"\\\\|heartbeatFn\\\\|isHeartbeat' ../agent-source/net_transport.go; sed -n '230,325p' ../agent-source/configuration.go; sed -n '667,712p' ../agent-source/raft.go; sed -n '930,965p' ../agent-source/raft.go; cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/tasks/audit.md\"","aggregated_output":"// verifyFuture is used to verify the current node is still\n// the leader. This is to prevent a stale read.\ntype verifyFuture struct {\n\tdeferError\n\tnotifyCh   chan *verifyFuture\n\tquorumSize int\n\tvotes      int\n\tvoteLock   sync.Mutex\n}\n\n// leadershipTransferFuture is used to track the progress of a leadership\n// transfer internally.\ntype leadershipTransferFuture struct {\n\tdeferError\n\n\tID      *ServerID\n\tAddress *ServerAddress\n}\n\n// configurationsFuture is used to retrieve the current configurations. This is\n// used to allow safe access to this information outside of the main thread.\ntype configurationsFuture struct {\n\tdeferError\n\tconfigurations configurations\n}\n\n// Configuration returns the latest configuration in use by Raft.\nfunc (c *configurationsFuture) Configuration() Configuration {\n\treturn c.configurations.latest\n}\n\n// Index returns the index of the latest configuration in use by Raft.\nfunc (c *configurationsFuture) Index() uint64 {\n\treturn c.configurations.latestIndex\n}\n\n// vote is used to respond to a verifyFuture.\n// This may block when responding on the notifyCh.\nfunc (v *verifyFuture) vote(leader bool) {\n\tv.voteLock.Lock()\n\tdefer v.voteLock.Unlock()\n\n\t// Guard against having notified already\n\tif v.notifyCh == nil {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif leader {\n\t\tv.votes++\n\t\tif v.votes >= v.quorumSize {\n\t\t\tv.notifyCh <- v\n\t\t\tv.notifyCh = nil\n\t\t}\n\t} else {\n\t\tv.notifyCh <- v\n\t\tv.notifyCh = nil\n\t}\n}\n\n// appendFuture is used for waiting on a pipelined append\n// entries RPC.\ntype appendFuture struct {\n\tdeferError\n\tstart time.Time\n\targs  *AppendEntriesRequest\n\tresp  *AppendEntriesResponse\n}\n\nfunc (a *appendFuture) Start() time.Time {\n\treturn a.start\nfunc (r *Raft) requestPreVote(rpc RPC, req *RequestPreVoteRequest) {\n\tdefer metrics.MeasureSince([]string{\"raft\", \"rpc\", \"requestVote\"}, time.Now())\n\tr.observe(*req)\n\n\t// Setup a response\n\tresp := &RequestPreVoteResponse{\n\t\tRPCHeader: r.getRPCHeader(),\n\t\tTerm:      r.getCurrentTerm(),\n\t\tGranted:   false,\n\t}\n\tvar rpcErr error\n\tdefer func() {\n\t\trpc.Respond(resp, rpcErr)\n\t}()\n\n\t// Check if we have an existing leader [who's not the candidate] and also\n\tcandidate := r.trans.DecodePeer(req.GetRPCHeader().Addr)\n\tcandidateID := ServerID(req.ID)\n\n\t// if the Servers list is empty that mean the cluster is very likely trying to bootstrap,\n\t// Grant the vote\n\tif len(r.configurations.latest.Servers) > 0 && !inConfiguration(r.configurations.latest, candidateID) {\n\t\tr.logger.Warn(\"rejecting pre-vote request since node is not in configuration\",\n\t\t\t\"from\", candidate)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif leaderAddr, leaderID := r.LeaderWithID(); leaderAddr != \"\" && leaderAddr != candidate {\n\t\tr.logger.Warn(\"rejecting pre-vote request since we have a leader\",\n\t\t\t\"from\", candidate,\n\t\t\t\"leader\", leaderAddr,\n\t\t\t\"leader-id\", string(leaderID))\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\t// Ignore an older term\n\tif req.Term < r.getCurrentTerm() {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif req.Term > r.getCurrentTerm() {\n\t\t// continue processing here to possibly grant the pre-vote as in a \"real\" vote this will transition us to follower\n\t\tr.logger.Debug(\"received a requestPreVote with a newer term, grant the pre-vote\")\n\t\tresp.Term = req.Term\n\t}\n\n\t// if we get a request for a pre-vote from a nonVoter  and the request term is higher, do not grant the Pre-Vote\n\t// This could happen when a node, previously voter, is converted to non-voter\n\tif len(r.configurations.latest.Servers) > 0 && !hasVote(r.configurations.latest, candidateID) {\n\t\tr.logger.Warn(\"rejecting pre-vote request since node is not a voter\", \"from\", candidate)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\t// Reject if their term is older\n\tlastIdx, lastTerm := r.getLastEntry()\n\tif lastTerm > req.LastLogTerm {\n\t\tr.logger.Warn(\"rejecting pre-vote request since our last term is greater\",\n\t\t\t\"candidate\", candidate,\n\t\t\t\"last-term\", lastTerm,\n\t\t\t\"last-candidate-term\", req.LastLogTerm)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif lastTerm == req.LastLogTerm && lastIdx > req.LastLogIndex {\n\t\tr.logger.Warn(\"rejecting pre-vote request since our last index is greater\",\n\t\t\t\"candidate\", candidate,\n\t\t\t\"last-index\", lastIdx,\n\t\t\t\"last-candidate-index\", req.LastLogIndex)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tresp.Granted = true\n}\n\n// installSnapshot is invoked when we get a InstallSnapshot RPC call.\n// We must be in the follower state for this, since it means we are\n// too far behind a leader for log replay. This must only be called\n// from the main thread.\nfunc (r *Raft) leadershipTransfer(id ServerID, address ServerAddress, repl *followerReplication, stopCh chan struct{}, doneCh chan error) {\n\t// make sure we are not already stopped\n\tselect {\n\tcase <-stopCh:\n\t\tdoneCh <- nil\n\t\treturn\n\tdefault:\n\t}\n\n\tfor atomic.LoadUint64(&repl.nextIndex) <= r.getLastIndex() {\n\t\terr := &deferError{}\n\t\terr.init()\n\t\trepl.triggerDeferErrorCh <- err\n\t\tselect {\n\t\tcase err := <-err.errCh:\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tdoneCh <- err\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}\n\t\tcase <-stopCh:\n\t\t\tdoneCh <- nil\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Step ?: the thesis describes in chap 6.4.1: Using clocks to reduce\n\t// messaging for read-only queries. If this is implemented, the lease\n\t// has to be reset as well, in case leadership is transferred. This\n\t// implementation also has a lease, but it serves another purpose and\n\t// doesn't need to be reset. The lease mechanism in our raft lib, is\n\t// setup in a similar way to the one in the thesis, but in practice\n\t// it's a timer that just tells the leader how often to check\n\t// heartbeats are still coming in.\n\n\t// Step 3: send TimeoutNow message to target server.\n\terr := r.trans.TimeoutNow(id, address, &TimeoutNowRequest{RPCHeader: r.getRPCHeader()}, &TimeoutNowResponse{})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\terr = fmt.Errorf(\"failed to make TimeoutNow RPC to %v: %v\", id, err)\n\t}\n\tdoneCh <- err\n}\n\n// checkLeaderLease is used to check if we can contact a quorum of nodes\n// within the last leader lease interval. If not, we need to step down,\n// as we may have lost connectivity. Returns the maximum duration without\n// contact. This must only be called from the main thread.\nfunc (r *Raft) preElectSelf() <-chan *preVoteResult {\n\n\t// At this point transport should support pre-vote\n\t// but check just in case\n\tprevoteTrans, prevoteTransSupported := r.trans.(WithPreVote)\n\tif !prevoteTransSupported {\n\t\tpanic(\"preElection is not possible if the transport don't support pre-vote\")\n\t}\n\n\t// Create a response channel\n\trespCh := make(chan *preVoteResult, len(r.configurations.latest.Servers))\n\n\t// Propose the next term without actually changing our state\n\tnewTerm := r.getCurrentTerm() + 1\n\n\t// Construct the request\n\tlastIdx, lastTerm := r.getLastEntry()\n\treq := &RequestPreVoteRequest{\n\t\tRPCHeader:    r.getRPCHeader(),\n\t\tTerm:         newTerm,\n\t\tLastLogIndex: lastIdx,\n\t\tLastLogTerm:  lastTerm,\n\t}\n\n\t// Construct a function to ask for a vote\n\taskPeer := func(peer Server) {\n\t\tr.goFunc(func() {\n\t\t\tdefer metrics.MeasureSince([]string{\"raft\", \"candidate\", \"preElectSelf\"}, time.Now())\n\t\t\tresp := &preVoteResult{voterID: peer.ID}\n\n\t\t\terr := prevoteTrans.RequestPreVote(peer.ID, peer.Address, req, &resp.RequestPreVoteResponse)\n\n\t\t\t// If the target server do not support Pre-vote RPC we count this as a granted vote to allow\n\t\t\t// the cluster to progress.\n\t\t\tif err != nil && strings.Contains(err.Error(), rpcUnexpectedCommandError) {\n\t\t\t\tr.logger.Error(\"target does not support pre-vote RPC, treating as granted\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"target\", peer,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"error\", err,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"term\", req.Term)\n\t\t\t\tresp.Term = req.Term\n\t\t\t\tresp.Granted = true\n\t\t\t} else if err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tr.logger.Error(\"failed to make requestVote RPC\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"target\", peer,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"error\", err,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"term\", req.Term)\n\t\t\t\tresp.Term = req.Term\n\t\t\t\tresp.Granted = false\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\trespCh <- resp\n\n\t\t})\n\t}\n\n\t// For each peer, request a vote\n\tfor _, server := range r.configurations.latest.Servers {\n\t\tif server.Suffrage == Voter {\n\t\t\tif server.ID == r.localID {\n\t\t\t\tr.logger.Debug(\"pre-voting for self\", \"term\", req.Term, \"id\", r.localID)\n\n\t\t\t\t// cast a pre-vote for our self\n\t\t\t\trespCh <- &preVoteResult{\n\t\t\t\t\tRequestPreVoteResponse: RequestPreVoteResponse{\n\t\t\t\t\t\tRPCHeader: r.getRPCHeader(),\n\t\t\t\t\t\tTerm:      req.Term,\n\t\t\t\t\t\tGranted:   true,\n\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\tvoterID: r.localID,\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tr.logger.Debug(\"asking for pre-vote\", \"term\", req.Term, \"from\", server.ID, \"address\", server.Address)\n\t\t\t\taskPeer(server)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\treturn respCh\n}\n\n// persistVote is used to persist our vote for safety.\nfunc (r *Raft) persistVote(term uint64, candidate []byte) error {\nfunc (r *Raft) pickServer() *Server {\n\tvar pick *Server\n\tvar current uint64\n\tfor _, server := range r.configurations.latest.Servers {\n\t\tif server.ID == r.localID || server.Suffrage != Voter {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tstate, ok := r.leaderState.replState[server.ID]\n\t\tif !ok {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tnextIdx := atomic.LoadUint64(&state.nextIndex)\n\t\tif nextIdx > current {\n\t\t\tcurrent = nextIdx\n\t\t\ttmp := server\n\t\t\tpick = &tmp\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn pick\n}\n\n// initiateLeadershipTransfer starts the leadership on the leader side, by\n// sending a message to the leadershipTransferCh, to make sure it runs in the\n// mainloop.\nfunc (r *Raft) initiateLeadershipTransfer(id *ServerID, address *ServerAddress) LeadershipTransferFuture {\n\tfuture := &leadershipTransferFuture{ID: id, Address: address}\n\tfuture.init()\n\n\tif id != nil && *id == r.localID {\n\t\terr := fmt.Errorf(\"cannot transfer leadership to itself\")\n\t\tr.logger.Info(err.Error())\n\t\tfuture.respond(err)\n\t\treturn future\n\t}\n\n\tselect {\n\tcase r.leadershipTransferCh <- future:\n\t\treturn future\n\tcase <-r.shutdownCh:\n\t\treturn errorFuture{ErrRaftShutdown}\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn errorFuture{ErrEnqueueTimeout}\n\t}\n}\n\n// timeoutNow is what happens when a server receives a TimeoutNowRequest.\nfunc (r *Raft) timeoutNow(rpc RPC, req *TimeoutNowRequest) {\n\tr.setLeader(\"\", \"\")\n\tr.setState(Candidate)\n\tr.candidateFromLeadershipTransfer.Store(true)\n\trpc.Respond(&TimeoutNowResponse{}, nil)\n}\n\n// setLatestConfiguration stores the latest configuration and updates a copy of it.\nfunc (r *Raft) setLatestConfiguration(c Configuration, i uint64) {\n\tr.configurations.latest = c\n\tr.configurations.latestIndex = i\n\tr.latestConfiguration.Store(c.Clone())\n}\n\n// setCommittedConfiguration stores the committed configuration.\nfunc (r *Raft) setCommittedConfiguration(c Configuration, i uint64) {\n\tr.configurations.committed = c\n\tr.configurations.committedIndex = i\n}\n\n// getLatestConfiguration reads the configuration from a copy of the main\n// configuration, which means it can be accessed independently from the main\n// loop.\nfunc (r *Raft) getLatestConfiguration() Configuration {\n\t// this switch catches the case where this is called without having set\n\t// a configuration previously.\n\tswitch c := r.latestConfiguration.Load().(type) {\n\tcase Configuration:\n\t\treturn c\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn Configuration{}\n87:\theartbeatFn     func(RPC)\n88:\theartbeatFnLock sync.Mutex\n194:func (n *netConn) Release() error {\n211:func NewNetworkTransportWithConfig(\n251:func NewNetworkTransport(\n273:func NewNetworkTransportWithLogger(\n285:func (n *NetworkTransport) setupStreamContext() {\n292:func (n *NetworkTransport) getStreamContext() context.Context {\n301:func (n *NetworkTransport) SetHeartbeatHandler(cb func(rpc RPC)) {\n302:\tn.heartbeatFnLock.Lock()\n303:\tdefer n.heartbeatFnLock.Unlock()\n304:\tn.heartbeatFn = cb\n308:func (n *NetworkTransport) CloseStreams() {\n333:func (n *NetworkTransport) Close() error {\n346:func (n *NetworkTransport) Consumer() <-chan RPC {\n351:func (n *NetworkTransport) LocalAddr() ServerAddress {\n356:func (n *NetworkTransport) IsShutdown() bool {\n366:func (n *NetworkTransport) getPooledConn(target ServerAddress) *netConn {\n383:func (n *NetworkTransport) getConnFromAddressProvider(id ServerID, target ServerAddress) (*netConn, error) {\n388:func (n *NetworkTransport) getProviderAddressOrFallback(id ServerID, target ServerAddress) ServerAddress {\n403:func (n *NetworkTransport) getConn(target ServerAddress) (*netConn, error) {\n434:func (n *NetworkTransport) returnConn(conn *netConn) {\n450:func (n *NetworkTransport) AppendEntriesPipeline(id ServerID, target ServerAddress) (AppendPipeline, error) {\n468:func (n *NetworkTransport) AppendEntries(id ServerID, target ServerAddress, args *AppendEntriesRequest, resp *AppendEntriesResponse) error {\n473:func (n *NetworkTransport) RequestVote(id ServerID, target ServerAddress, args *RequestVoteRequest, resp *RequestVoteResponse) error {\n478:func (n *NetworkTransport) RequestPreVote(id ServerID, target ServerAddress, args *RequestPreVoteRequest, resp *RequestPreVoteResponse) error {\n483:func (n *NetworkTransport) genericRPC(id ServerID, target ServerAddress, rpcType uint8, args interface{}, resp interface{}) error {\n509:func (n *NetworkTransport) InstallSnapshot(id ServerID, target ServerAddress, args *InstallSnapshotRequest, resp *InstallSnapshotResponse, data io.Reader) error {\n547:func (n *NetworkTransport) EncodePeer(id ServerID, p ServerAddress) []byte {\n553:func (n *NetworkTransport) DecodePeer(buf []byte) ServerAddress {\n558:func (n *NetworkTransport) TimeoutNow(id ServerID, target ServerAddress, args *TimeoutNowRequest, resp *TimeoutNowResponse) error {\n563:func (n *NetworkTransport) listen() {\n606:func (n *NetworkTransport) handleConn(connCtx context.Context, conn net.Conn) {\n639:func (n *NetworkTransport) handleCommand(r *bufio.Reader, dec *codec.Decoder, enc *codec.Encoder) error {\n660:\tisHeartbeat := false\n679:\t\t\tisHeartbeat = true\n682:\t\tif isHeartbeat {\n725:\tif isHeartbeat {\n726:\t\tn.heartbeatFnLock.Lock()\n727:\t\tfn := n.heartbeatFn\n728:\t\tn.heartbeatFnLock.Unlock()\n771:func decodeResponse(conn *netConn, resp interface{}) (bool, error) {\n793:func sendRPC(conn *netConn, rpcType uint8, args interface{}) error {\n817:func newNetPipeline(trans *NetworkTransport, conn *netConn, maxInFlight int) *netPipeline {\n841:func (n *netPipeline) decodeResponses() {\n864:func (n *netPipeline) AppendEntries(args *AppendEntriesRequest, resp *AppendEntriesResponse) (AppendFuture, error) {\n894:func (n *netPipeline) Consumer() <-chan AppendFuture {\n899:func (n *netPipeline) Close() error {\n\t\treturn Configuration{}, fmt.Errorf(\"configuration changed since %v (latest is %v)\", change.prevIndex, currentIndex)\n\t}\n\n\tconfiguration := current.Clone()\n\tswitch change.command {\n\tcase AddVoter:\n\t\tnewServer := Server{\n\t\t\tSuffrage: Voter,\n\t\t\tID:       change.serverID,\n\t\t\tAddress:  change.serverAddress,\n\t\t}\n\t\tfound := false\n\t\tfor i, server := range configuration.Servers {\n\t\t\tif server.ID == change.serverID {\n\t\t\t\tif server.Suffrage == Voter {\n\t\t\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers[i].Address = change.serverAddress\n\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers[i] = newServer\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tfound = true\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !found {\n\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers = append(configuration.Servers, newServer)\n\t\t}\n\tcase AddNonvoter:\n\t\tnewServer := Server{\n\t\t\tSuffrage: Nonvoter,\n\t\t\tID:       change.serverID,\n\t\t\tAddress:  change.serverAddress,\n\t\t}\n\t\tfound := false\n\t\tfor i, server := range configuration.Servers {\n\t\t\tif server.ID == change.serverID {\n\t\t\t\tif server.Suffrage != Nonvoter {\n\t\t\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers[i].Address = change.serverAddress\n\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers[i] = newServer\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tfound = true\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !found {\n\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers = append(configuration.Servers, newServer)\n\t\t}\n\tcase DemoteVoter:\n\t\tfor i, server := range configuration.Servers {\n\t\t\tif server.ID == change.serverID {\n\t\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers[i].Suffrage = Nonvoter\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\tcase RemoveServer:\n\t\tfor i, server := range configuration.Servers {\n\t\t\tif server.ID == change.serverID {\n\t\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers = append(configuration.Servers[:i], configuration.Servers[i+1:]...)\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\tcase Promote:\n\t\tfor i, server := range configuration.Servers {\n\t\t\tif server.ID == change.serverID && server.Suffrage == Staging {\n\t\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers[i].Suffrage = Voter\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Make sure we didn't do something bad like remove the last voter\n\tif err := checkConfiguration(configuration); err != nil {\n\t\treturn Configuration{}, err\n\t}\n\n\treturn configuration, nil\n}\n\n// encodePeers is used to serialize a Configuration into the old peers format.\n// This is here for backwards compatibility when operating with a mix of old\n// servers and should be removed once we deprecate support for protocol version 1.\nfunc encodePeers(configuration Configuration, trans Transport) []byte {\n\t// Gather up all the voters, other suffrage types are not supported by\n\t// this data format.\n\tvar encPeers [][]byte\n\tfor _, server := range configuration.Servers {\n\t\tif server.Suffrage == Voter {\n\t\t\tencPeers = append(encPeers, trans.EncodePeer(server.ID, server.Address))\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Encode the entire array.\n\tbuf, err := encodeMsgPack(encPeers)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tpanic(fmt.Errorf(\"failed to encode peers: %v\", err))\n\t}\nfunc (r *Raft) leaderLoop() {\n\t// stepDown is used to track if there is an inflight log that\n\t// would cause us to lose leadership (specifically a RemovePeer of\n\t// ourselves). If this is the case, we must not allow any logs to\n\t// be processed in parallel, otherwise we are basing commit on\n\t// only a single peer (ourself) and replicating to an undefined set\n\t// of peers.\n\tstepDown := false\n\t// This is only used for the first lease check, we reload lease below\n\t// based on the current config value.\n\tlease := time.After(r.config().LeaderLeaseTimeout)\n\n\tfor r.getState() == Leader {\n\t\tr.mainThreadSaturation.sleeping()\n\n\t\tselect {\n\t\tcase rpc := <-r.rpcCh:\n\t\t\tr.mainThreadSaturation.working()\n\t\t\tr.processRPC(rpc)\n\n\t\tcase <-r.leaderState.stepDown:\n\t\t\tr.mainThreadSaturation.working()\n\t\t\tr.setState(Follower)\n\n\t\tcase future := <-r.leadershipTransferCh:\n\t\t\tr.mainThreadSaturation.working()\n\t\t\tif r.getLeadershipTransferInProgress() {\n\t\t\t\tr.logger.Debug(ErrLeadershipTransferInProgress.Error())\n\t\t\t\tfuture.respond(ErrLeadershipTransferInProgress)\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tr.logger.Debug(\"starting leadership transfer\", \"id\", future.ID, \"address\", future.Address)\n\n\t\t\t// When we are leaving leaderLoop, we are no longer\n\t\t\t// leader, so we should stop transferring.\n\t\t\tleftLeaderLoop := make(chan struct{})\n\t\t\tdefer func() { close(leftLeaderLoop) }()\n\n\t\t\tstopCh := make(chan struct{})\n\t\t\tdoneCh := make(chan error, 1)\n\n\t\t\t// This is intentionally being setup outside of the\n\t\t\t// leadershipTransfer function. Because the TimeoutNow\n\t\t\t// call is blocking and there is no way to abort that\n\t\t\t// in case eg the timer expires.\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tr.dispatchLogs(ready)\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\tcase <-lease:\n\t\t\tr.mainThreadSaturation.working()\n\t\t\t// Check if we've exceeded the lease, potentially stepping down\n\t\t\tmaxDiff := r.checkLeaderLease()\n\n\t\t\t// Next check interval should adjust for the last node we've\n\t\t\t// contacted, without going negative\n\t\t\tcheckInterval := r.config().LeaderLeaseTimeout - maxDiff\n\t\t\tif checkInterval < minCheckInterval {\n\t\t\t\tcheckInterval = minCheckInterval\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t// Renew the lease timer\n\t\t\tlease = time.After(checkInterval)\n\n\t\tcase <-r.leaderNotifyCh:\n\t\t\tfor _, repl := range r.leaderState.replState {\n\t\t\t\tasyncNotifyCh(repl.notifyCh)\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\tcase <-r.followerNotifyCh:\n\t\t\t//  Ignore since we are not a follower\n\n\t\tcase <-r.shutdownCh:\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\n// verifyLeader must be called from the main thread for safety.\n// Causes the followers to attempt an immediate heartbeat.\nfunc (r *Raft) verifyLeader(v *verifyFuture) {\n# File products for one audit investigation\n\nRead research.json for selected work and shared relationship navigation. A record locator names an existing JSON path, collection and exact match fields; paths are relative to the index directory unless absolute. Select matching records, then read field when present. Historical previews are navigation, not current pending work. Use artifact basis locators and graph_versions for old requirements, not the latest same-ID claim. Materials and execution IDs resolve through records in state.json. Full reviews, drafts and fixed inputs remain at their indexed paths.\n\nWhen capacity permits, supply an optional short Chinese report_title and one to three report_answer sentences in review items, leading with the measured discrepancy and actual observation. State decisive applicability once and keep open disputes visible; leave repeated execution detail and wider exclusions in the scoped records. Keep English semantic reasoning; actual verdicts and measurements prevail. Omission never blocks work or warrants a translation turn.\n\nWrite a complete submission.json using submission.schema.json and product-schemas.json. Cite authorized captured ranges. Follow next_objective and the analysis guide for core_overview readiness; a usable map and first Candidate may share a submission.\n\nWhen repairing a rejected product, set repair_of to its operation_id and submit the whole product. Diagnostics retain ownership: reconsider=submission calls for product repair; reconsider=research_decision requires a different research action, not field repair of an unauthorized stop. Repeated errors may pause only the draft, never unrelated questions.\n\n- continue / pause / explained / obligation: select candidate_id or fork using parent_candidate_id, with a complete current question. Sourced feedback may refine the discriminator before its first obligation; later requirement/scope changes use F2/F3. A fork explains holds/violated/incomplete effects on its parent. Pause supplies resume_conditions; explained cites the protective mechanism. Obligation supplies one attributed claim and source bindings. A complete check may be combined now, or constructed later.\n- check / revise_check: select unit_id (or its Candidate alias), or create an obligation through candidate. Supply plan_path, draft-source harness_path and optional destination-to-draft files; plan.harness.execution_package may select one Go package or Rust crate for this check. Metadata source/files stay empty; the controller fixes executable bytes and adapter support. Never replace target code or dependencies. Revisions name previous_check_id. Driver legality repairs name repair_issue_ids and explain changed inputs and sources; reference every removed conflict's exact issue. Changed executed checker encoding uses encoding_revision. Removing an extra property needs an exact open correspondence issue whose sourced scope/oracle review names out_of_scope_checker_ids; preserve every retained predicate and all harness inputs, then execute and review the explicit successor. Changing the obligation itself still uses F2/F3.\n- research: submit substantive feedback alone with acquired source or retained execution ref_ids, or a complete partial map_path, additive graph_path or scope_path. Feedback alone needs no Candidate or usable overview and creates no map version or Evidence. An identical adjacent pure handoff on unchanged research receives duplicate_of: accepted without new knowledge; continue useful investigation, not rewording. A map may accompany one graph/scope operation. semantic_revision supplies an attributed F2/F3 feedback_path for an existing unit_id and may carry a map. Graph additions cannot invent unowned executable Units.\n- review: select artifact_id; omitted item target_id inherits it. Carries feedback, not a map. Use review_contracts/review_questions: Direct Check requires checker_correspondence; other aspects are optional unless resolving an issue of that aspect. revision_needed names challenged_components. Resolve exact issue_ids using acquired Material source_ids, a concise answer and retained evidence_ids when relevant. For supplied conditions, use condition_dispositions with exact condition_id, sources and applicability; current_judgment remains unresolved. Unchanged sources and reasoning can be referenced, not recopied. The review guide defines semantic criteria. Candidate applicability review creates no execution Evidence.\n- explore: submit a question, draft-source harness_path, optional files and optional execution_package with the same meaning as Harness.execution_package. Clean-copy output guides construction without property Evidence.\n- stop: candidate/family/focus release local work; unfinished Units and disputes remain. A local tool/resource gap supplies resume_conditions. Focus releases unfinished research while preserving explained/closed/paused dispositions and each question's own conditions; shared focus reasons stay in this stop record. Open runs reject scope=run: continue with research, exploration or another Candidate within remaining authorization. Only a preconfigured finite directed_question may end with run/bounded_completed after its task is disposed; cite the explained, closed or checked Candidate. Cancellation, permission/service failure and exhausted time/calls are controller events, never submission authority.\n\nFor Go, omit execution_package to retain the run default package and main-file destination. An explicit local directory selects that package and places the primary file there using the configured basename. Helpers in files remain relative to the workspace root. The controller fixes the effective package and bytes before execution; it runs Go directly in a clean copy, without a root launcher. Select only one existing package in the captured module; paths, patterns, nested modules, workspaces and dependency overrides cannot expand authorization. Python does not support this override.\n\nFor Rust, execution_package selects one captured crate directory and tests/<configured basename>.rs, with workspace-relative helpers. Use research.build_inputs (fixed lock, tools, metadata and selected-test compilation) to check available APIs against effective features; a source declaration alone does not establish active cfg or public reachability. Original manifests and dev-dependencies determine features; no extra flags are added. Omit logging or helper initialization unrelated to the discriminator. The backend instructions describe private seed reuse and current harness execution; preparation consumes the run deadline and supplies no observations. Never replace manifests, locks, build scripts or tool configuration.\n\nA formal question names one principal fact_ids entry, lifecycle, direct behavior_ids, sourced A1/A2 relationship, contexts, event_paths, importance and trigger_rationale. supporting_behavior_ids maps distinct Behavior IDs to their causal role. audit_spec_version may be omitted for the current basis. A map file's version is its accepted base (1 initially); the controller assigns resulting versions, including questions in combined products and F2/F3 patches. Do not guess current+1. Unchanged Candidates retain their historical basis. A supporting-layer question cites its actual consumer or core relationship and declares the supported A1/A2 activity; a local storage obligation need not become a whole-cluster consequence. If that relationship lacks sources, investigate or retain feedback instead of inventing a core label.\n\nThe controller derives actual map differences and reverse indexes. map_changes explains modified/removed objects and new producers or consumers of an existing principal Fact, with impact (clarification/meaning/dependency), acquired source_ids and rationale. Use one preserves explanation for unchanged requirements, dependencies and observation scope, or challenges mapping saved Candidate IDs to specific disputed premises. A corrected principal Fact requires a challenge; clarification cannot disguise identity/context/edge changes or removal. Independent additions need no invented revision and may still challenge a prior interpretation.\n\nCoherent knowledge and its issues are accepted together; unaffected checks retain their basis. reconnect_questions updates explicitly selected questions. ScopeUpdate/F3 expands dependencies under its existing write rules; changed normative or fault/configuration applicability uses F2. No-op maps create no version.\n\nFor every feedback shape, including one accompanying a map, Candidate or review, ref_ids directly includes each saved CheckRun whose execution it explains, alongside relevant Candidate, Behavior, Fact, surface:<entry_point> and Material IDs. Obtain execution IDs from research.json.explorations[*].executions[*].check_id or the exact records locator, not operation/plan IDs or prose. Explaining only a repaired execution references only that run; a joint explanation references both failure and repair and distinguishes their observations. Shared sources, Behavior or harness names do not associate executions. Source-only answers need no execution reference. Map/map_changes source_ids remain Material references. understanding records learning, not a map change; use the guide's natural handoff. question_updates revises Candidate unknowns/resume_conditions with sources, retaining requirements and counterevidence. Historical remaining is then-remaining; current execution/review records remain authoritative.\n\nClaim/Scope owns requirement and applicability; Harness legality records this history and caller duties. Use the experiments reference for predicate correspondence, observation synchronization, prerequisite waits and cleanup responsibility during construction and review. Unreached setup retains its observation and calls for minimal repair preserving the discriminator. claim.concern classifies responsibility, not confidence.\n\nOptional preflight: run validation.command followed by the draft-relative filename in an existing Codex tool call. It shares acceptance preparation, writes no accepted state and executes no target; formal submission rechecks fixed bytes and current state without a preflight ticket or reserved budget. research.json capacity and preflight elapsed_seconds describe saved run checkpoints, not live time within this turn. Use the controller's current turn allocation and referenced CheckRun for the actual time basis; its estimated UTC deadline is explanatory and the runner enforces the hard timeout. new_obligation is an entry capability, not a complete check/review budget; remaining.agent_calls counts future turns, not local work in this running turn.\n\nOnce a sourced product independently expresses substantive research progress, you may return it and continue in the next turn. Initial delivery need not wait for a Candidate, obligation, harness or all local trials. Before the two-line overview and its connection are usable, retain real partial understanding through research feedback or a partial map; do not claim full readiness. Combine products when ready. Passing preflight does not force immediate submission, but further expansion should serve a concrete new discriminator within the remaining turn time. A feedback-only exploration answer retains conditions, observations and open responsibility/history/endpoint questions under the same reference rule. Keep rejected larger drafts and diagnostics separate; the small product neither repairs nor partially accepts them. There is no required first-turn product, separate feedback turn or delivery quota. A reliable completion receipt fixes only declared product files before deadline handling; saved bytes are not acceptance or Evidence. Without that receipt, drafts remain unsubmitted. Natural expiry needs no closing submission.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'))['\"'$defs'\"']['CandidateSubmission'];print(json.dumps(s,indent=2))\nPY\nsed -n '638,700p' ../agent-source/net_transport.go\nsed -n '220,305p' ../agent-source/configuration.go\nsed -n '667,700p' ../agent-source/raft.go\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'))['\"'$defs'\"']['CandidateSubmission'];print(json.dumps(s,indent=2))\nPY\nsed -n '638,700p' ../agent-source/net_transport.go\nsed -n '220,305p' ../agent-source/configuration.go\nsed -n '667,700p' ../agent-source/raft.go\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"rationale\": {\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Rationale\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"sources\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SourceRange\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Sources\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"feedback\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ResearchFeedback\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null\n    },\n    \"repair_of\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"description\": \"Rejected operation ID whose complete draft this submission repairs\",\n      \"title\": \"Repair Of\"\n    },\n    \"map_path\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Map Path\"\n    },\n    \"map_changes\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/UnderstandingChange\"\n      },\n      \"default\": {},\n      \"title\": \"Map Changes\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"reconnect_questions\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/AuditQuestion\"\n      },\n      \"description\": \"Optional explicit question reconnections; changing an accepted Unit proposition still requires F2/F3\",\n      \"title\": \"Reconnect Questions\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"action\": {\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"continue\",\n        \"pause\",\n        \"explained\",\n        \"obligation\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Action\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"candidate_id\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Candidate Id\"\n    },\n    \"parent_candidate_id\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Parent Candidate Id\"\n    },\n    \"question\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/AuditQuestion\"\n    },\n    \"resume_conditions\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Resume Conditions\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"result_implications\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"default\": {},\n      \"propertyNames\": {\n        \"enum\": [\n          \"holds\",\n          \"violated\",\n          \"incomplete\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Result Implications\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"obligation\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ClaimDraft\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null\n    },\n    \"bindings\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/BindingDraft\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Bindings\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"rationale\",\n    \"action\",\n    \"question\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"CandidateSubmission\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n// handleCommand is used to decode and dispatch a single command.\nfunc (n *NetworkTransport) handleCommand(r *bufio.Reader, dec *codec.Decoder, enc *codec.Encoder) error {\n\tgetTypeStart := time.Now()\n\n\t// Get the rpc type\n\trpcType, err := r.ReadByte()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\n\t// measuring the time to get the first byte separately because the heartbeat conn will hang out here\n\t// for a good while waiting for a heartbeat whereas the append entries/rpc conn should not.\n\tmetrics.MeasureSince([]string{\"raft\", \"net\", \"getRPCType\"}, getTypeStart)\n\tdecodeStart := time.Now()\n\n\t// Create the RPC object\n\trespCh := make(chan RPCResponse, 1)\n\trpc := RPC{\n\t\tRespChan: respCh,\n\t}\n\n\t// Decode the command\n\tisHeartbeat := false\n\tvar labels []metrics.Label\n\tswitch rpcType {\n\tcase rpcAppendEntries:\n\t\tvar req AppendEntriesRequest\n\t\tif err := dec.Decode(&req); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\trpc.Command = &req\n\n\t\tleaderAddr := req.RPCHeader.Addr\n\t\tif len(leaderAddr) == 0 {\n\t\t\tleaderAddr = req.Leader\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t// Check if this is a heartbeat\n\t\tif req.Term != 0 && leaderAddr != nil &&\n\t\t\treq.PrevLogEntry == 0 && req.PrevLogTerm == 0 &&\n\t\t\tlen(req.Entries) == 0 && req.LeaderCommitIndex == 0 {\n\t\t\tisHeartbeat = true\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tif isHeartbeat {\n\t\t\tlabels = []metrics.Label{{Name: \"rpcType\", Value: \"Heartbeat\"}}\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tlabels = []metrics.Label{{Name: \"rpcType\", Value: \"AppendEntries\"}}\n\t\t}\n\tcase rpcRequestVote:\n\t\tvar req RequestVoteRequest\n\t\tif err := dec.Decode(&req); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\trpc.Command = &req\n\t\tlabels = []metrics.Label{{Name: \"rpcType\", Value: \"RequestVote\"}}\n\tcase rpcRequestPreVote:\n\t\tvar req RequestPreVoteRequest\n\t\tif err := dec.Decode(&req); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\trpc.Command = &req\n\t\tlabels = []metrics.Label{{Name: \"rpcType\", Value: \"RequestPreVote\"}}\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"need at least one voter in configuration: %v\", configuration)\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// nextConfiguration generates a new Configuration from the current one and a\n// configuration change request. It's split from appendConfigurationEntry so\n// that it can be unit tested easily.\nfunc nextConfiguration(current Configuration, currentIndex uint64, change configurationChangeRequest) (Configuration, error) {\n\tif change.prevIndex > 0 && change.prevIndex != currentIndex {\n\t\treturn Configuration{}, fmt.Errorf(\"configuration changed since %v (latest is %v)\", change.prevIndex, currentIndex)\n\t}\n\n\tconfiguration := current.Clone()\n\tswitch change.command {\n\tcase AddVoter:\n\t\tnewServer := Server{\n\t\t\tSuffrage: Voter,\n\t\t\tID:       change.serverID,\n\t\t\tAddress:  change.serverAddress,\n\t\t}\n\t\tfound := false\n\t\tfor i, server := range configuration.Servers {\n\t\t\tif server.ID == change.serverID {\n\t\t\t\tif server.Suffrage == Voter {\n\t\t\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers[i].Address = change.serverAddress\n\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers[i] = newServer\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tfound = true\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !found {\n\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers = append(configuration.Servers, newServer)\n\t\t}\n\tcase AddNonvoter:\n\t\tnewServer := Server{\n\t\t\tSuffrage: Nonvoter,\n\t\t\tID:       change.serverID,\n\t\t\tAddress:  change.serverAddress,\n\t\t}\n\t\tfound := false\n\t\tfor i, server := range configuration.Servers {\n\t\t\tif server.ID == change.serverID {\n\t\t\t\tif server.Suffrage != Nonvoter {\n\t\t\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers[i].Address = change.serverAddress\n\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers[i] = newServer\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tfound = true\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !found {\n\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers = append(configuration.Servers, newServer)\n\t\t}\n\tcase DemoteVoter:\n\t\tfor i, server := range configuration.Servers {\n\t\t\tif server.ID == change.serverID {\n\t\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers[i].Suffrage = Nonvoter\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\tcase RemoveServer:\n\t\tfor i, server := range configuration.Servers {\n\t\t\tif server.ID == change.serverID {\n\t\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers = append(configuration.Servers[:i], configuration.Servers[i+1:]...)\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\tcase Promote:\n\t\tfor i, server := range configuration.Servers {\n\t\t\tif server.ID == change.serverID && server.Suffrage == Staging {\n\t\t\t\tconfiguration.Servers[i].Suffrage = Voter\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Make sure we didn't do something bad like remove the last voter\n\tif err := checkConfiguration(configuration); err != nil {\n\t\treturn Configuration{}, err\n\t}\n\n\treturn configuration, nil\nfunc (r *Raft) leaderLoop() {\n\t// stepDown is used to track if there is an inflight log that\n\t// would cause us to lose leadership (specifically a RemovePeer of\n\t// ourselves). If this is the case, we must not allow any logs to\n\t// be processed in parallel, otherwise we are basing commit on\n\t// only a single peer (ourself) and replicating to an undefined set\n\t// of peers.\n\tstepDown := false\n\t// This is only used for the first lease check, we reload lease below\n\t// based on the current config value.\n\tlease := time.After(r.config().LeaderLeaseTimeout)\n\n\tfor r.getState() == Leader {\n\t\tr.mainThreadSaturation.sleeping()\n\n\t\tselect {\n\t\tcase rpc := <-r.rpcCh:\n\t\t\tr.mainThreadSaturation.working()\n\t\t\tr.processRPC(rpc)\n\n\t\tcase <-r.leaderState.stepDown:\n\t\t\tr.mainThreadSaturation.working()\n\t\t\tr.setState(Follower)\n\n\t\tcase future := <-r.leadershipTransferCh:\n\t\t\tr.mainThreadSaturation.working()\n\t\t\tif r.getLeadershipTransferInProgress() {\n\t\t\t\tr.logger.Debug(ErrLeadershipTransferInProgress.Error())\n\t\t\t\tfuture.respond(ErrLeadershipTransferInProgress)\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tr.logger.Debug(\"starting leadership transfer\", \"id\", future.ID, \"address\", future.Address)\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"The notification path has no voter check: every registered peer can increment the verification count, and reaching that count makes the leader loop return success. The lease check does filter for voters, so it is relevant counterevidence. I’ll retain this as a candidate with an open discriminator: can nonvoter replies complete verification when voter support is unavailable, and what does the API contract require in that history?"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_submission.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nsources=[]\ndef src(i,f,a,b,k='code_observation'):\n sources.append(dict(id=i,file=f,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind=k));return i\nsrc('s_commit','commitment.go',11,104)\nsrc('s_run','raft.go',135,259)\nsrc('s_election','raft.go',285,440)\nsrc('s_leader','raft.go',455,650)\nsrc('s_config_gate','raft.go',650,665)\nsrc('s_loop','raft.go',667,963)\nsrc('s_verify','raft.go',965,987)\nsrc('s_lease','raft.go',1031,1094)\nsrc('s_dispatch','raft.go',1203,1388)\nsrc('s_append','raft.go',1390,1600)\nsrc('s_votes','raft.go',1603,1808)\nsrc('s_install','raft.go',1814,1954)\nsrc('s_campaign','raft.go',1976,2150)\nsrc('s_transfer','raft.go',990,1030)\nsrc('s_state','raft.go',2152,2239)\nsrc('s_repl','replication.go',137,385)\nsrc('s_heartbeat','replication.go',388,441)\nsrc('s_pipeline','replication.go',534,631)\nsrc('s_match','replication.go',646,668)\nsrc('s_notify','replication.go',98,119)\nsrc('s_verify_future','future.go',236,296)\nsrc('s_start','api.go',500,706)\nsrc('s_client','api.go',804,895,'interface_statement')\nsrc('s_fsm','fsm.go',15,44,'interface_statement')\nsrc('s_fsm_run','fsm.go',83,264)\nsrc('s_members','configuration.go',8,82,'interface_statement')\nsrc('s_config_update','configuration.go',225,305)\nsrc('s_store','log.go',110,148,'interface_statement')\nsrc('s_stable','stable.go',6,18,'interface_statement')\nsrc('s_net_hb','net_transport.go',638,682)\nB=[]\ndef beh(i,a,owner,ctx,trig,ss,**kw):\n b=dict(id=i,primary_activity=a,execution_owner=owner,protocol_context=ctx,trigger=trig,source_ids=ss);b.update(kw);B.append(b)\nbeh('b_election','A2','Raft main loop and per-peer vote RPC goroutines','Local term, latest configuration, log/snapshot tip','Follower timeout, candidate retry, or TimeoutNow', ['s_run','s_election','s_campaign','s_votes','s_state'],implementation_guards=['Only configured voters are solicited; majority is derived from latest voter count.','RequestVote checks term, candidate membership/suffrage where ID is supplied, existing leader, prior vote and log freshness; persists vote before granting.','Pre-vote does not persist or advance local term; successful pre-vote starts a real election.'],writes=['Real election persists incremented term and self vote; majority grants establish Leader state.'],async_boundaries=['Each campaign has a fresh buffered response channel; old RPC replies remain on the old channel after candidate exit.'],important_branches=['Newer response term causes fallback; inbound append or higher-term vote may change role; timeout restarts campaign.','Leadership transfer bypasses pre-vote and permits vote despite known leader; flag resets when runCandidate returns.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Chosen leader creates a new commitment context and begins with a no-op.'})\nbeh('b_leader_context','A2','Raft main loop','One leadership tenure and term','runLeader entry and deferred exit',['s_leader','s_loop','s_lease'],writes=['Fresh commitment, replication map, inflight queue and verification set on entry.'],external_effects=['Dispatch initial no-op; lease loss or stale-term notification causes stepdown.','Exit closes replicator stop channels and responds ErrLeadershipLost to remaining inflight and verification futures.'],async_boundaries=['Each followerReplication retains the commitment and stepDown channel of its original tenure; late replies do not target newly allocated leader accounting.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'startIndex is lastIndex+1 and prevents committing old-term support before a current-term entry is replicated.','A7':'Leadership loss is ambiguous for writes; it is not rollback of durable entries.'})\nbeh('b_dispatch','A1','Leader main loop','Leader term and inflight log index','Client apply batch, initial no-op, or configuration entry',['s_dispatch','s_loop'],writes=['Assign sequential indexes and current term; enqueue futures; successful StoreLogs updates cached last log.'],durable_effects=['StoreLogs before local commitment.match.'],external_effects=['Successful storage notifies each replicator; failure responds errors and sets Follower.'],produces_fact_ids=['f_match'],unknowns=['appendConfigurationEntry continues updating configuration after dispatchLogs returns on storage failure; consequences and store fault contract need investigation.'])\nbeh('b_replicate','A1','Per-peer replication and pipeline decoding goroutines','Peer ID and captured leader term/commitment','New-log trigger, periodic commit propagation, retry, pipeline result',['s_repl','s_pipeline','s_match'],implementation_guards=['Successful AppendEntries response is required for match update; higher response term signals old leader stepdown.'],writes=['Success updates nextIndex and match at last request entry; rejection backs nextIndex down; missing log selects snapshot recovery.'],async_boundaries=['Transport response belongs to the issued request; pipeline responses expose Request and Response together.'],produces_fact_ids=['f_match'],cross_activity_effects={'A3':'Missing historical entries switches to InstallSnapshot; its success reports snapshot index match.'})\nbeh('b_commit','A1','Commitment mutex; leader main loop consumer','Current leadership commitment and latest voter set','match, setConfiguration, then commitCh',['s_commit','s_loop'],implementation_guards=['Only voter IDs present in matchIndexes can advance their monotonic match index.','Sorted majority index must exceed current commitment and reach startIndex.'],writes=['Commitment advances and coalesces commitCh notification; leader consumes it into commitIndex.'],consumes_fact_ids=['f_match'],produces_fact_ids=['f_commit'],external_effects=['Leader queues committed inflight entries for FSM and marks configuration committed; removal of local vote triggers stepdown.'])\nbeh('b_append','A1','Main RPC loop; heartbeat fast path has restricted empty requests','Follower local term, stored prefix and leader commit index','Incoming AppendEntries',['s_append','s_net_hb','s_start'],implementation_guards=['Older terms rejected; newer terms persisted and role changed; ordinary same-term append also steps down except transfer candidate.','Previous index/term must match; duplicate terms skipped; conflicting suffix deleted before replacement append.'],writes=['Successful replacement updates cached last log and latest configuration; conflict rolls latest configuration back to committed.','Leader commit propagation advances to min(leaderCommit,lastIndex) and queues unapplied logs.'],durable_effects=['StoreLogs precedes successful append acknowledgment.'],important_branches=['StoreLogs failure after successful DeleteRange returns failure without updating cached lastLog; explicit TODO recognizes this state.','Fast heartbeat requires zero previous index/term, no entries and zero leaderCommit at NetworkTransport classifier.'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Append reception establishes leader contact and can invalidate candidate/leader authority.','A4':'Conflict truncation can discard an uncommitted configuration.'},unknowns=['Can cached tip survive a truncate/store failure and be consumed as if durable on a later legal append or vote?'])\nbeh('b_config','A4','Raft main loop','Latest and committed configuration indexes','Configuration API request or configuration entry processing',['s_config_gate','s_config_update','s_dispatch','s_append','s_members','s_leader'],implementation_guards=['Leader admits a new change only when latest configuration is committed and a current-term entry is committed.','nextConfiguration checks prevIndex when nonzero and validates resulting configuration.'],writes=['Configuration entry immediately updates latest configuration, commitment voter membership and replication targets.','setConfiguration retains old match index for surviving voter IDs, defaults new voters to zero.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Voter set determines eligible matches and majority threshold.','A2':'Latest voter set determines campaigns, lease checks and leader removal.'})\nbeh('b_recover','A3','Construction thread before startup; RPC main loop and FSM restore goroutine for remote snapshot','Durable term/log/snapshot and configuration','NewRaft or InstallSnapshot',['s_start','s_install','s_repl','s_fsm_run'],implementation_guards=['Startup loads term and log tip, restores a usable snapshot and scans subsequent log entries for configuration.','InstallSnapshot rejects old terms/version mismatch and size mismatch; waits on FSM restore future before reporting success.'],writes=['Restore sets lastApplied, lastSnapshot and both configuration views.'],durable_effects=['Received snapshot sink is finalized before FSM restore.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Snapshot provides prefix for lagging replicas; leader counts snapshot match after success.','A2':'Recovered log/snapshot tip is used in freshness checks; restored latest configuration determines eligibility.'},unknowns=['Ordering and freshness of delayed snapshots relative to already applied entries need separate legal-history analysis.'])\nbeh('b_persist','A6','Raft vote and term setters','Current term and last vote keys in injected StableStore','setCurrentTerm and persistVote',['s_campaign','s_stable','s_votes'],durable_effects=['setCurrentTerm writes durable term before atomic memory state, panicking on error.','persistVote writes term key then candidate key; requestVote grants only if both succeed.'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Durable vote tuple prevents multiple candidates being granted votes in the same term on normal successful storage paths.'},unknowns=['Partial two-key vote persistence failure/crash behavior and applicable storage error assumptions remain unexamined.'])\nbeh('b_apply','A5','Main processLogs producer; dedicated runFSM consumer','Committed log index and FSM queue','Commit processing or follower commit propagation',['s_dispatch','s_fsm_run','s_fsm'],consumes_fact_ids=['f_commit'],writes=['processLogs ignores already queued indexes, queues commands/barriers/configurations as appropriate, then sets lastApplied.','runFSM serially invokes Apply or ApplyBatch and responds to matching futures after application; restore and snapshot requests share FSM owner.'],async_boundaries=['lastApplied records queueing by main loop, not necessarily completed application; future response is a separate endpoint.'],cross_activity_effects={'A7':'Apply response and Barrier completion reflect FSM processing rather than just majority storage.'})\nbeh('b_client','A7','Caller and main-loop admission','API invocation and future','ApplyLog, Barrier, VerifyLeader',['s_client','s_loop','s_run','s_election'],external_effects=['Enqueue timeout is distinct from completion; followers and candidates reject leader operations.','VerifyLeader enqueues a verifyFuture; leader loop responds success when returned count reaches configured quorum.'],consumes_fact_ids=['f_verify_tally'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'VerifyLeader is publicly described as preventing stale reads after leadership loss.'})\nbeh('b_verify_register','A2','Leader main loop','One verifyFuture within a leader tenure','verifyCh initial request invokes verifyLeader',['s_verify','s_leader','s_lease'],writes=['Sets votes=1 for self and quorumSize from latest voter count; one-voter case succeeds immediately.','Registers future in every replication state, including nonvoters, and triggers heartbeat.'],produces_fact_ids=['f_verify_tally'],unknowns=['No suffrage filter is visible on registration despite voter-only quorum size.'])\nbeh('b_verify_notify','A2','Per-peer heartbeat/replication goroutines; verifyFuture voteLock','Registered verifyFuture and each replication notification map','Heartbeat or successful replication/snapshot notification',['s_notify','s_verify_future','s_heartbeat','s_match','s_repl'],writes=['notifyAll swaps out per-peer pending map under notifyLock; vote(true) increments count under voteLock.','At threshold or first rejection, vote sends future to verifyCh and clears notifyCh; later votes ignored.'],produces_fact_ids=['f_verify_tally'],consumes_fact_ids=['f_verify_tally'],important_branches=['Non-error heartbeat updates lastContact and votes response.Success without checking suffrage.','Transport errors supply no vote; replication higher term calls notifyAll(false) and signals stepdown.'])\nbeh('b_verify_consume','A2','Leader main loop','Completed tally for current tracked verifyFuture','verifyCh returns future with nonzero quorumSize',['s_loop','s_verify_future'],consumes_fact_ids=['f_verify_tally'],external_effects=['Count below quorum causes stepdown and ErrNotLeader; count at quorum produces nil error; pending per-peer notifications are cleaned.'],unknowns=['Whether the count can represent only self plus nonvoters in an admitted history, and thus fail the public authority-check responsibility.'])\nbeh('b_transfer','A2','Leader loop with transfer goroutine; target main loop','Selected follower and transfer interval','LeadershipTransfer or TimeoutNow',['s_transfer','s_state','s_loop','s_election'],implementation_guards=['Default target is most advanced other voter; replication is brought through current tip before TimeoutNow.'],external_effects=['Leader loop restricts new writes during transfer; target enters Candidate with transfer flag; completion is coordinated with leader loop exit or timeout.'],unknowns=['Explicit-target eligibility and transfer cleanup under overlapping removal/shutdown need deeper investigation.'])\nF=[dict(id='f_match',meaning='For each tracked voter ID the current commitment object retains the highest index reported through its match interface; this accounting is used as durable prefix support, not independent verification of storage.',identity={'tenure':'commitment object','voter':'ServerID'},validity_context='Current leader commitment object and configured voter membership; surviving voter values carry across setConfiguration.',representation=['commitment.matchIndexes'],durability='Volatile; based on successful local storage, append response or snapshot response.',recovery='Fresh leader commitment starts all voter matches at zero.',source_ids=['s_commit','s_dispatch','s_repl','s_match']),dict(id='f_commit',meaning='The leader commitment object has advanced to an index supported by its voter-majority match calculation and at least its current-term startIndex.',identity={'tenure':'commitment object'},validity_context='Current leadership tenure and membership used for recalculation; monotonic within object.',representation=['commitment.commitIndex','commitCh'],durability='Volatile derivation from stored replication support.',recovery='New leadership rederives through a current-term no-op; startup restores snapshot and log history.',source_ids=['s_commit','s_leader','s_start']),dict(id='f_verify_tally',meaning='A verifyFuture contains the initial self count plus positive notifications delivered through registered replication states before the first terminal notification. This is a notification count, not an assertion that counted peers are voters.',identity={'operation':'verifyFuture pointer'},validity_context='One verification registered during leader tenure, with quorumSize fixed at registration; notifyCh nil ends collection.',representation=['verifyFuture.votes','verifyFuture.quorumSize','verifyFuture.notifyCh'],durability='Volatile per-operation state.',recovery='No replay; pending tracked requests receive leadership-loss response on leader exit.',source_ids=['s_verify','s_notify','s_verify_future','s_loop','s_leader'])]\nroles=json.load(open('../research.json'))['activity_roles']\nactivities=[]\nfor a,role in roles.items():\n bs=[b for b in B if b['primary_activity']==a]\n activities.append(dict(class_id=a,applicability='applicable',purpose=role['relation'],realization_summary={'A1':'Leader durable appends and per-peer support feed voter-majority commitment; followers accept consistent history and propagated commit indexes.','A2':'Term-based campaigns and persisted votes acquire authority; inbound terms, lease checks, transfer and role exit govern loss. Verification uses a separate notification tally.','A3':'Startup reconstructs from log and snapshot; lagging replication installs a snapshot and resumes appends.','A4':'Logged configuration determines voter eligibility; latest and committed views support bounded configuration transition and rollback.','A5':'Committed entries queue to a serialized FSM owner; future completion follows application.','A6':'LogStore, StableStore and snapshot interfaces hold durable history and term/vote context; concrete store implementations remain to be reviewed.','A7':'Client APIs enqueue work and return futures; rejection, leadership loss and FSM completion have distinct meanings.'}[a],behavior_ids=[b['id'] for b in bs],source_ids=list(dict.fromkeys(s for b in bs for s in b['source_ids']))))\ndef path(ex,bs,ss,fs=[]):return dict(explanation=ex,behavior_ids=bs,source_ids=ss,fact_ids=fs)\nm=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured Go raft package implementing replicated log, elections, configuration, snapshot recovery and client futures; caller supplies FSM, stores and transport. In-repository transports and stores remain in scope, not externalized merely because injected.',protocol_contexts=['ServerID and address','Persistent term and log/snapshot tip','Latest and committed voter configurations','Per-leader commitment and per-operation verifyFuture'],external_interfaces=['Transport RPCs','LogStore and StableStore','SnapshotStore','FSM and optional BatchingFSM/ConfigurationStore','Apply/Barrier/VerifyLeader and configuration APIs'],ownership=['Main Raft loop','Per-peer replication/heartbeat goroutines','FSM goroutine','Snapshot goroutine'],variants=['Pre-vote conditional on transport support/config','Legacy protocol compatibility','Batching FSM','MonotonicLogStore'],source_ids=['s_start','s_members','s_client','s_store','s_stable','s_fsm']),activities=activities,behaviors=B,facts=F,surfaces=[dict(entry_point='Raft.appendEntries truncation followed by StoreLogs failure',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b_append'],reason='Failure return preserves stale cached lastLog after durable suffix removal. Need establish legal retry/election history and storage fault contract before an obligation.',source_ids=['s_append','s_store'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Raft.verifyLeader nonvoter notifications',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b_verify_register','b_verify_notify','b_verify_consume'],reason='Voter-derived threshold is fed by all registered replication peers; selected for next discriminator.',source_ids=['s_verify','s_notify','s_verify_future'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Raft.restoreUserSnapshot',disposition='deferred',reason='Distinct user restore history and pending-write abortion require deeper caller contract and resynchronization reading.',source_ids=['s_client','s_loop'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='NetworkTransport heartbeat fast path',disposition='deferred',reason='Classifier limits heartbeat mutation, but concurrent term/role ownership and shutdown dispatch deserve separate analysis.',source_ids=['s_net_hb','s_start','s_append'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='StableStore vote tuple failure',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b_persist'],reason='Two-key persistence has an unresolved crash/error atomicity premise.',source_ids=['s_campaign','s_stable'],high_consequence=True)],core_overview=dict(status='usable',formation=path('A1: main-loop leader dispatch assigns index/term and stores entries, then local storage and successful per-peer append/snapshot replies report matches to a tenure-specific commitment. Only configured voter IDs enter the majority calculation; advancement must reach a current-term entry. The leader consumes commitCh and queues committed entries to FSM; ordinary AppendEntries carries commit index to followers, including periodic propagation when writes cease. Followers check previous log term, replace conflicts, and queue committed entries; runFSM responds after actual application.',['b_dispatch','b_replicate','b_commit','b_append','b_apply'],['s_dispatch','s_repl','s_commit','s_append','s_fsm_run'],['f_match','f_commit']),context=path('A2: follower timeout starts a configured-voter campaign, with optional pre-vote, persistent real term/self vote and per-campaign response channel. RequestVote combines membership, term, durable vote and log freshness guards. A majority enters Leader, allocating fresh replication/commitment state and dispatching a no-op. Higher-term RPC/reply, failed voter contact lease, committed removal or transfer can end authority. Exit stops old replication and fails outstanding futures; old replies retain old channels/commitment. TimeoutNow starts a transfer campaign; the transfer flag resets at campaign exit.',['b_election','b_leader_context','b_persist','b_transfer'],['s_run','s_election','s_votes','s_campaign','s_leader','s_lease','s_transfer','s_state']),connection=path('Previously stored entries survive role changes; new leaders rederive commitment under a fresh current-term barrier rather than inheriting match counts. Latest logged membership controls support eligibility, campaigns and lease quorum; leader configuration changes are serialized behind prior configuration commitment and current-term commitment, while follower truncation can restore committed membership. Startup loads term and log tip, restores snapshot/configuration and scans newer configuration entries; those histories constrain future votes and replication. VerifyLeader is a separate authority-consumption path: a voter-derived quorum threshold is compared with notifications from replication peers, an unresolved qualification discrepancy rather than a proved authority guarantee.',['b_leader_context','b_config','b_recover',