erify_consume'],fact_ids=['f_verify_tally'],supporting_behavior_ids={'b_config':'Determines actual voter membership and replication population.','b_leader_context':'Lease checks and role exit can invalidate the request before completion.','b_election':'A competing leader history would determine whether a stale-authority consequence is reachable.','b_client':'Public API defines authority-check use and exposes future result.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['The periodic leader lease counts only voters and can force stepdown; a schedule must account for its timing instead of disabling it to claim the public endpoint.','Log commitment already filters match support by voter ID, so this discrepancy alone does not establish unsafe log commitment.','A failed verification reply or leader exit can return an error before positive notifications complete.'],unknowns=['Does an independently constructed legal registration/delivery history yield a completed verification tally from self plus nonvoters without voter replies?','What precise local qualification obligation is supported by the public VerifyLeader contract and voter semantics, and is a competing-leader history needed for the chosen proposition?','Can a public endpoint witness retain ordinary lease/transport behavior and all caller completion duties?'],priority=3,trigger_rationale='Source shows voter-only quorumSize but unconditional registration of all replication peers and identity-free vote increment; notification path supplies no suffrage filter. This is more specific than generic variant coverage. First resolve the local qualification contract and construct a small count witness; only then choose whether a full authority-history test is necessary.',disposition='concrete_suspicion',preferred_check='source_review')\nsub=dict(action='continue',rationale='Save the initial two-core relationship map and select the sourced VerifyLeader support-eligibility discrepancy; no defect or execution result is presumed.',sources=sources,map_path='map.json',question=q,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['s_verify','s_notify','s_verify_future','s_lease','s_append','s_store'],answered='The normal commitment path filters voters and uses fresh per-term accounting. Verification is separate: verifyLeader registers all replication states, notifyAll forwards boolean support without suffrage, and vote counts it against a voter-derived threshold. The voter-only lease is a separate possible protection, not a filter on this count. A second source lead is cached lastLog left unchanged on replacement StoreLogs failure after conflict truncation.',remaining=q['unknowns'],understanding='updated',rationale='Save source-derived selection and contrary protection together; no test has run and no violation is asserted.'))\njson.dump(sub,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 build_submission.py\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\ncmd=json.load(open('../research.json'))['validation']['command']\nr=subprocess.run(cmd+['submission.json'],capture_output=True,text=True)\nprint(r.stdout);print(r.stderr)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": false, \"run_id\": \"5988999a91fe4f62b5bd585d09c0beb5\", \"audit_spec_version\": 0, \"elapsed_seconds\": 0.7067048429998977, \"diagnostics\": [{\"details\": {\"blocked_checks\": \"Checks requiring this excerpt await valid source bytes\"}, \"code\": \"source_range\", \"category\": \"material\", \"task\": \"\", \"candidate_version\": 0, \"object_ids\": [\"s_match\"], \"paths\": [\"/sources/18\"], \"material_ids\": [], \"message\": \"Source citation range does not exist: s_match\", \"allowed\": [\"read\", \"representation\"]}, {\"details\": {}, \"code\": \"core_overview\", \"category\": \"semantic\", \"task\": \"\", \"candidate_version\": 0, \"object_ids\": [], \"paths\": [\"/core_overview/context\"], \"material_ids\": [], \"message\": \"A usable path needs explanation and Behavior, Fact and source references\", \"allowed\": [\"read\", \"semantic_revision\"